IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`

-- coa25-names-ch1.l4: Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom), Part 41 "Business names", Chapter 1 "Restricted or
-- prohibited names": ss 1192 to 1199A (lines 16783-16915 of ukpga-2006-46.txt). Layer 1: the law, objectively.
--
-- SOURCE. A plain-text rendering of the Act from legislation.gov.uk made by a converter script; it is not the
-- official text and nothing here is "verified against the official text". Quote lines are checked by srcrefs.py.
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER (the rule of 2026-10-29, assumed, not ruled by a lawyer; NOTES.md, "Reading a result").
--   JUST TRUE   the text says yes (for a "contravenes" function: every element of the prohibition is present).
--   JUST FALSE  the text says no in its own words: -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "<quoted words>"
--   NOTHING     the text does not decide: -- NOTHING-kind (<why>), <why> being one of: silent, list not closed,
--               includes, undefined term, points outside the text, limited by its own wording.
--   A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- Answers other parts give are INPUTS under the names PLAN.md section 4 gives them (s 1121, s 57A, s 73, ...).
-- Every name below begins with the section label it implements.
--
-- Regulation-making powers and their procedure (ss 1193(3), 1194(2), 1195(1), 1197(1), (2) and (4)) are inert, reason 2.
-- Findings (NOTES.md): s 1199(1) lists ss 1192 to 1196 and s 1197 but not s 1196A (the foreign-government prohibition added
-- later) and not the prohibitions of ss 1198 to 1198B; s 1198A(5) and s 1198B(7) define "relevant direction" by two
-- different lists of sections (1198A(5) names s 76, 1198B(7) does not).

§ `Part 41: business names`

§§ `Chapter 1: restricted or prohibited names`

-- ---- s 1192: Application of this Chapter ------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:16786 | 1192 Application of this Chapter
-- src:16787 | (1) Subject to any express provision to the contrary, this Chapter applies to any person carrying on business in the United Kingdom.
@ref s 1192(1) Application of this Chapter (src:16786-16787)
GIVEN `the person is carrying on business in the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an express provision to the contrary applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1192(1) this Chapter applies to the person` MEANS
    IF NOT `the person is carrying on business in the United Kingdom`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "this Chapter applies to any person carrying on business in the United Kingdom" (a scope limit with no "only": the 2026-11-05 ruling)
    ELSE IF `an express provision to the contrary applies`
         THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "Subject to any express provision to the contrary": the provision that provides to the contrary decides
         ELSE JUST TRUE

DECLARE `s 1192 kind of business` IS ONE OF
    `s 1192 an individual carrying on business`
    `s 1192 individuals carrying on business in partnership`
    `s 1192 another person carrying on business`

DECLARE `s 1192 addition` IS ONE OF
    `s 1192 an individual's forename or initial`
    `s 1192 the forenames of individual partners or the initials of those forenames`
    `s 1192 the addition of "s" at the end of a surname shared by two or more individual partners`
    `s 1192 an addition merely indicating that the business is carried on in succession to a former owner of the business`
    `s 1192 any other addition`

-- src:16791 | (3) The following are the permitted additions—
-- src:16792 | (a) in the case of an individual, his forename or initial;
-- src:16793 | (b) in the case of a partnership—
-- src:16794 | (i) the forenames of individual partners or the initials of those forenames, or
-- src:16795 | (ii) where two or more individual partners have the same surname, the addition of “s” at the end of that surname;
-- src:16796 | (c) in either case, an addition merely indicating that the business is carried on in succession to a former owner of the business.
@ref s 1192(3) The permitted additions (src:16791-16796)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 1192 kind of business`
      addition IS A `s 1192 addition`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1192(3) the addition is a permitted addition` MEANS
    CONSIDER addition
    WHEN `s 1192 an individual's forename or initial` THEN
        CONSIDER kind
        WHEN `s 1192 an individual carrying on business` THEN JUST TRUE -- (a)
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) in the case of an individual, his forename or initial" (a list the text hands the definition to: the 2026-11-05 ruling)
    WHEN `s 1192 the forenames of individual partners or the initials of those forenames` THEN
        CONSIDER kind
        WHEN `s 1192 individuals carrying on business in partnership` THEN JUST TRUE -- (b)(i)
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) in the case of a partnership— (i) the forenames of individual partners or the initials of those forenames"
    WHEN `s 1192 the addition of "s" at the end of a surname shared by two or more individual partners` THEN
        CONSIDER kind
        WHEN `s 1192 individuals carrying on business in partnership` THEN JUST TRUE -- (b)(ii)
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) in the case of a partnership— ... (ii) where two or more individual partners have the same surname, the addition of “s” at the end of that surname"
    WHEN `s 1192 an addition merely indicating that the business is carried on in succession to a former owner of the business` THEN
        CONSIDER kind
        WHEN `s 1192 another person carrying on business` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(c) in either case": either an individual or a partnership
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE -- (c)
    WHEN `s 1192 any other addition` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The following are the permitted additions" (a list the text hands the definition to: the 2026-11-05 ruling)

-- src:16788 | (2) The provisions of this Chapter do not prevent—
-- src:16789 | (a) an individual carrying on business under a name consisting of his surname without any addition other than a permitted addition, or
-- src:16790 | (b) individuals carrying on business in partnership under a name consisting of the surnames of all the partners without any addition other than a permitted addition.
@ref s 1192(2) The Chapter does not prevent a business name consisting of the surname or surnames with permitted additions (src:16788-16790)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 1192 kind of business`
      `the name consists of his surname (an individual) or of the surnames of all the partners (individuals in partnership)` IS A BOOLEAN
      additions IS A LIST OF `s 1192 addition`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1192(2) this Chapter prevents the business name` MEANS
    IF kind EQUALS `s 1192 another person carrying on business`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(a) an individual carrying on business ... (b) individuals carrying on business in partnership"
    ELSE IF `the name consists of his surname (an individual) or of the surnames of all the partners (individuals in partnership)`
            AND all (GIVEN a YIELD `s 1192(3) the addition is a permitted addition` kind a EQUALS JUST TRUE) additions
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The provisions of this Chapter do not prevent— (a) an individual carrying on business under a name consisting of his surname without any addition other than a permitted addition, or (b) individuals carrying on business in partnership under a name consisting of the surnames of all the partners without any addition other than a permitted addition"
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the flat negative reaches only a name consisting of the surname or surnames with permitted additions; the sections that follow decide the rest

-- ---- s 1193: Name suggesting connection with government or public authority ------------------------------------

DECLARE `s 1193 body the name would suggest a connection with` IS ONE OF
    `s 1193 Her Majesty's Government, a part of the Scottish administration, the Welsh Assembly Government or Her Majesty's Government in Northern Ireland`
    `s 1193 a local authority`
    `s 1193 a public authority specified for the purposes of this section by regulations made by the Secretary of State`
    `s 1193 no such body`

-- src:16798 | 1193 Name suggesting connection with government or public authority
-- src:16799 | (1) A person must not, without the approval of the Secretary of State, carry on business in the United Kingdom under a name that would be likely to give the impression that the business is connected with—
-- src:16800 | (a) Her Majesty's Government, any part of the Scottish administration , the Welsh Assembly Government or Her Majesty's Government in Northern Ireland,
-- src:16801 | (b) any local authority, or
-- src:16802 | (c) any public authority specified for the purposes of this section by regulations made by the Secretary of State.
@ref s 1193(1) Name suggesting connection with government or public authority (src:16798-16802)
GIVEN `the person carries on business in the United Kingdom under the name` IS A BOOLEAN
      body IS A `s 1193 body the name would suggest a connection with`
      `the name would be likely to give the impression that the business is connected with that body` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the approval of the Secretary of State has been given` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1199 sections 1192 to 1197 do not apply to the business` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 1199A(1) the prohibitions of this Chapter do not apply to the business under the name` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1193(1) the person contravenes the prohibition on a name suggesting connection with government or a public authority` MEANS
    IF `s 1199 sections 1192 to 1197 do not apply to the business` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Those sections do not apply to the carrying on of a business by a person who— (a) carried on the business immediately before the date on which this Chapter came into force" (s 1199(2))
    ELSE IF `s 1199A(1) the prohibitions of this Chapter do not apply to the business under the name` EQUALS JUST TRUE
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "provide that a prohibition imposed by this Chapter does not apply in relation to the carrying on of a business by that person under a name specified in the notice" (s 1199A(1))
         ELSE IF NOT `the person carries on business in the United Kingdom under the name`
              THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "carry on business in the United Kingdom under a name"
              ELSE CONSIDER body
                   WHEN `s 1193 no such body` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "that the business is connected with— (a) Her Majesty's Government ..., (b) any local authority, or (c) any public authority specified"
                   OTHERWISE
                       IF NOT `the name would be likely to give the impression that the business is connected with that body`
                       THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a name that would be likely to give the impression"
                       ELSE IF `the approval of the Secretary of State has been given`
                            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "without the approval of the Secretary of State"
                            ELSE JUST TRUE

DECLARE `s 1193 description of local authority` IS ONE OF
    `s 1193 a local authority within the meaning of the Local Government Act 1972`
    `s 1193 the Common Council of the City of London`
    `s 1193 the Council of the Isles of Scilly`
    `s 1193 a council constituted under section 2 of the Local Government etc. (Scotland) Act 1994`
    `s 1193 a district council in Northern Ireland`
    `s 1193 another body`

-- src:16803 | (2) For the purposes of this section—
-- src:16804 | “local authority” means—
-- src:16805 | (a) a local authority within the meaning of the Local Government Act 1972 (c. 70), the Common Council of the City of London or the Council of the Isles of Scilly,
-- src:16806 | (b) a council constituted under section 2 of the Local Government etc. (Scotland) Act 1994 (c. 39), or
-- src:16807 | (c) a district council in Northern Ireland;
@ref s 1193(2) "Local authority" (src:16803-16807)
GIVEN description IS A `s 1193 description of local authority`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1193(2) the body is a local authority` MEANS
    CONSIDER description
    WHEN `s 1193 another body` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“local authority” means— (a) a local authority within the meaning of the Local Government Act 1972 (c. 70), the Common Council of the City of London or the Council of the Isles of Scilly, (b) a council constituted under section 2 of the Local Government etc. (Scotland) Act 1994 (c. 39), or (c) a district council in Northern Ireland"
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:16803 | (2) For the purposes of this section—
-- src:16808 | “public authority” includes any person or body having functions of a public nature.
@ref s 1193(2) "Public authority" (src:16803-16808)
GIVEN `the person or body has functions of a public nature` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1193(2) the person or body is a public authority` MEANS
    IF `the person or body has functions of a public nature`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“public authority” includes any person or body having functions of a public nature"

-- src:16810 | (4) A person who contravenes this section commits an offence.
@ref s 1193(4) Offence (src:16810)
GIVEN `the person contravenes the prohibition on a name suggesting connection with government or a public authority` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1193(4) the person commits an offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the person contravenes the prohibition on a name suggesting connection with government or a public authority`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person who contravenes this section commits an offence" (the offence is defined by the contravention: marginal reading (a))
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person contravenes is not known
-- src:16811 | (5) Where an offence under this section is committed by a body corporate, an offence is also committed by every officer of the body who is in default.
@ref s 1193(5) Offence: every officer of the body corporate who is in default (src:16811)
GIVEN `the body corporate commits an offence under this section` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1193(5) an officer of the body corporate commits an offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the body corporate commits an offence under this section`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an offence under this section is committed by a body corporate, an offence is also committed by every officer of the body who is in default" (a "where" that fails: the 2026-11-05 ruling)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the body corporate commits the offence is not known
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        CONSIDER `s 1121 the officer is in default`
        WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an offence is also committed by every officer of the body who is in default"
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the officer is in default is the answer of s 1121
-- src:16812 | (6) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 3 on the standard scale.
@ref s 1193(6) Penalty for an offence under s 1193 (src:16812)
GIVEN guilty IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 1193(6) the penalty for an offence under s 1193` MEANS
    CONSIDER guilty
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        JUST (Penalty WITH `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction`
                           `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING
                           `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 1)
                           `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 0.1)
                           `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE)
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person is guilty is not known

-- ---- s 1194: Other sensitive words or expressions --------------------------------------------------------

-- src:16813 | 1194 Other sensitive words or expressions
-- src:16814 | (1) A person must not, without the approval of the Secretary of State, carry on business in the United Kingdom under a name that includes a word or expression for the time being specified in regulations made by the Secretary of State under this section.
@ref s 1194(1) Other sensitive words or expressions (src:16813-16814)
GIVEN `the person carries on business in the United Kingdom under the name` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the name includes a word or expression for the time being specified in regulations made by the Secretary of State under s 1194` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the approval of the Secretary of State has been given` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1199 sections 1192 to 1197 do not apply to the business` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 1199A(1) the prohibitions of this Chapter do not apply to the business under the name` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1194(1) the person contravenes the prohibition on a name including a specified word or expression` MEANS
    IF `s 1199 sections 1192 to 1197 do not apply to the business` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Those sections do not apply to the carrying on of a business by a person who— (a) carried on the business immediately before the date on which this Chapter came into force" (s 1199(2))
    ELSE IF `s 1199A(1) the prohibitions of this Chapter do not apply to the business under the name` EQUALS JUST TRUE
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "provide that a prohibition imposed by this Chapter does not apply in relation to the carrying on of a business by that person under a name specified in the notice" (s 1199A(1))
         ELSE IF NOT `the person carries on business in the United Kingdom under the name`
              THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "carry on business in the United Kingdom under a name"
              ELSE IF NOT `the name includes a word or expression for the time being specified in regulations made by the Secretary of State under s 1194`
                   THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a name that includes a word or expression for the time being specified in regulations made by the Secretary of State under this section"
                   ELSE IF `the approval of the Secretary of State has been given`
                        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "without the approval of the Secretary of State"
                        ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:16816 | (3) A person who contravenes this section commits an offence.
@ref s 1194(3) Offence (src:16816)
GIVEN `the person contravenes the prohibition on a name including a specified word or expression` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1194(3) the person commits an offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the person contravenes the prohibition on a name including a specified word or expression`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person who contravenes this section commits an offence" (the offence is defined by the contravention: marginal reading (a))
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person contravenes is not known
-- src:16817 | (4) Where an offence under this section is committed by a body corporate, an offence is also committed by every officer of the body who is in default.
@ref s 1194(4) Offence: every officer of the body corporate who is in default (src:16817)
GIVEN `the body corporate commits an offence under this section` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1194(4) an officer of the body corporate commits an offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the body corporate commits an offence under this section`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an offence under this section is committed by a body corporate, an offence is also committed by every officer of the body who is in default" (a "where" that fails: the 2026-11-05 ruling)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the body corporate commits the offence is not known
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        CONSIDER `s 1121 the officer is in default`
        WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an offence is also committed by every officer of the body who is in default"
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the officer is in default is the answer of s 1121
-- src:16818 | (5) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 3 on the standard scale.
@ref s 1194(5) Penalty for an offence under s 1194 (src:16818)
GIVEN guilty IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 1194(5) the penalty for an offence under s 1194` MEANS
    CONSIDER guilty
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        JUST (Penalty WITH `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction`
                           `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING
                           `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 1)
                           `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 0.1)
                           `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE)
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable"
