-- ---- s 1195: Requirement to seek comments of government department or other relevant body ---------------------
-- Subsection (1) is a regulation-making power (inert, reason 2). Subsections (2) to (4) bite only "where such a
-- requirement applies" under the regulations.

-- src:16824 | (2) Where such a requirement applies, the applicant must request the specified department or other body (in writing) to indicate whether (and if so why) it has any objections to the proposed name.
@ref s 1195(2) The applicant must request the specified department or other body to indicate whether it has any objections (src:16824)
GIVEN `such a requirement applies under regulations made under s 1193 or s 1194` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicant has requested the specified department or other body, in writing, to indicate whether (and if so why) it has any objections to the proposed name` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1195(2) the applicant has complied with the requirement to request the view of the department or body` MEANS
    IF NOT `such a requirement applies under regulations made under s 1193 or s 1194`
    THEN JUST TRUE -- the duty does not engage, so nothing is left to fail (fork F5)
    ELSE IF `the applicant has requested the specified department or other body, in writing, to indicate whether (and if so why) it has any objections to the proposed name`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where such a requirement applies, the applicant must request the specified department or other body (in writing) to indicate whether (and if so why) it has any objections to the proposed name" (a bare "must" not done: decided at this site, fork F5)

-- src:16825 | (3) He must submit to the Secretary of State a statement that such a request has been made and a copy of any response received from the specified body.
@ref s 1195(3) The applicant must submit a statement that the request has been made and a copy of any response (src:16825)
GIVEN `such a requirement applies under regulations made under s 1193 or s 1194` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicant has submitted to the Secretary of State a statement that such a request has been made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a response was received from the specified body` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicant has submitted a copy of the response` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1195(3) the applicant has complied with the requirement to submit a statement and a copy of any response` MEANS
    IF NOT `such a requirement applies under regulations made under s 1193 or s 1194`
    THEN JUST TRUE -- the duty does not engage, so nothing is left to fail (fork F5)
    ELSE IF `the applicant has submitted to the Secretary of State a statement that such a request has been made`
            AND ((NOT `a response was received from the specified body`) OR `the applicant has submitted a copy of the response`)
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "He must submit to the Secretary of State a statement that such a request has been made and a copy of any response received from the specified body" (a bare "must" not done: decided at this site, fork F5)

-- src:16826 | (4) If these requirements are not complied with, the Secretary of State may refuse to consider the application for approval.
@ref s 1195(4) The Secretary of State may refuse to consider the application for approval (src:16826)
GIVEN `s 1195(2) the applicant has complied with the requirement to request the view of the department or body` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 1195(3) the applicant has complied with the requirement to submit a statement and a copy of any response` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1195(4) the Secretary of State may refuse to consider the application for approval` MEANS
    IF `s 1195(2) the applicant has complied with the requirement to request the view of the department or body` EQUALS JUST FALSE
       OR `s 1195(3) the applicant has complied with the requirement to submit a statement and a copy of any response` EQUALS JUST FALSE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If these requirements are not complied with, the Secretary of State may refuse to consider the application for approval"

-- src:16827 | (5) In this section “specified” means specified in the regulations.
@ref s 1195(5) "Specified" (src:16827)
GIVEN `the matter is specified in the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1195(5) the matter is specified` MEANS
    IF `the matter is specified in the regulations`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In this section “specified” means specified in the regulations"

DECLARE `s 1195 party` IS ONE OF
    `s 1195 the applicant for approval`

DECLARE `s 1195 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 1195 request the specified department or other body, in writing, to indicate whether it has any objections to the proposed name`
    `s 1195 submit to the Secretary of State a statement that the request has been made and a copy of any response`

-- src:16824 | (2) Where such a requirement applies, the applicant must request the specified department or other body (in writing) to indicate whether (and if so why) it has any objections to the proposed name.
-- src:16825 | (3) He must submit to the Secretary of State a statement that such a request has been made and a copy of any response received from the specified body.
@ref s 1195(2) The applicant must request the view of the department or body and then submit a statement and a copy of any response (src:16824-16825)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 1195 party` `s 1195 act`
`s 1195(2) the applicant must request the view of the department or body and submit a statement` MEANS
    PARTY `s 1195 the applicant for approval`
    MUST `s 1195 request the specified department or other body, in writing, to indicate whether it has any objections to the proposed name`
    HENCE (
        PARTY `s 1195 the applicant for approval`
        MUST `s 1195 submit to the Secretary of State a statement that the request has been made and a copy of any response`
        HENCE FULFILLED
        LEST BREACH BY `s 1195 the applicant for approval` BECAUSE "s 1195(3): no statement that the request was made, and no copy of any response, was submitted to the Secretary of State"
    )
    LEST BREACH BY `s 1195 the applicant for approval` BECAUSE "s 1195(2): the specified department or other body was not asked, in writing, whether it has any objections"

-- ---- s 1196: Withdrawal of Secretary of State's approval --------------------------------------------------

DECLARE `s 1196 approval` IS ONE OF
    `s 1196 an approval given for the purposes of s 1193 (name suggesting connection with government or public authority)`
    `s 1196 an approval given for the purposes of s 1194 (other sensitive words or expressions)`
    `s 1196 another approval`

-- src:16828 | 1196 Withdrawal of Secretary of State's approval
-- src:16829 | (1) This section applies to approval given for the purposes of—
-- src:16830 | section 1193 (name suggesting connection with government or public authority), or
-- src:16831 | section 1194 (other sensitive words or expressions).
-- src:16832 | (2) If it appears to the Secretary of State that there are overriding considerations of public policy that require such approval to be withdrawn, the approval may be withdrawn by notice in writing given to the person concerned.
@ref s 1196(2) Withdrawal of the Secretary of State's approval (src:16828-16832)
GIVEN approval IS A `s 1196 approval`
      `it appears to the Secretary of State that there are overriding considerations of public policy that require the approval to be withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1196(2) the approval may be withdrawn by notice in writing given to the person concerned` MEANS
    CONSIDER approval
    WHEN `s 1196 another approval` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section applies to approval given for the purposes of— section 1193 ... or section 1194"
    OTHERWISE
        IF `it appears to the Secretary of State that there are overriding considerations of public policy that require the approval to be withdrawn`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If it appears to the Secretary of State that there are overriding considerations of public policy that require such approval to be withdrawn, the approval may be withdrawn by notice in writing" (a power whose "if" gate is unmet: fork F28)

-- src:16833 | (3) The notice must state the date as from which approval is withdrawn.
@ref s 1196(3) The notice must state the date as from which approval is withdrawn (src:16833)
GIVEN `the notice states the date as from which approval is withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1196(3) the notice meets the requirement to state a date` MEANS
    IF `the notice states the date as from which approval is withdrawn`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The notice must state the date as from which approval is withdrawn" (a bare "must" not met: decided at this site, fork F5)

-- "as from" the date stated: the approval is withdrawn on that date and after it, not before.
-- src:16833 | (3) The notice must state the date as from which approval is withdrawn.
@ref s 1196(3) The notice must state the date as from which approval is withdrawn (src:16833)
GIVEN `the date stated in the notice as the date as from which approval is withdrawn` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the question is asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1196(3) the approval has been withdrawn` MEANS
    IF `the date on which the question is asked` AT LEAST `the date stated in the notice as the date as from which approval is withdrawn`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the date as from which approval is withdrawn" (a period the text fixes in its own words: the 2026-11-05 ruling)

-- ---- s 1196A: Names suggesting connection with foreign governments etc ------------------------------------

DECLARE `s 1196A body the name would falsely suggest a connection with` IS ONE OF
    `s 1196A a foreign government or an agency or authority of a foreign government`
    `s 1196A an international organisation whose members include two or more countries or territories (or their governments)`
    `s 1196A no such body`

-- src:16834 | 1196A Names suggesting connection with foreign governments etc
-- src:16835 | (1) A person must not carry on business in the United Kingdom under a name that would be likely to give the false impression that the business is connected with—
-- src:16836 | (a) a foreign government or an agency or authority of a foreign government, or
-- src:16837 | (b) an international organisation whose members include two or more countries or territories (or their governments).
@ref s 1196A(1) Names suggesting connection with foreign governments etc (src:16834-16837)
GIVEN `the person carries on business in the United Kingdom under the name` IS A BOOLEAN
      body IS A `s 1196A body the name would falsely suggest a connection with`
      `the name would be likely to give the false impression that the business is connected with that body` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1199A(1) the prohibitions of this Chapter do not apply to the business under the name` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1196A(1) the person contravenes the prohibition on a name suggesting connection with a foreign government or an international organisation` MEANS
    IF `s 1199A(1) the prohibitions of this Chapter do not apply to the business under the name` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "provide that a prohibition imposed by this Chapter does not apply in relation to the carrying on of a business by that person under a name specified in the notice" (s 1199A(1))
    ELSE IF NOT `the person carries on business in the United Kingdom under the name`
         THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "carry on business in the United Kingdom under a name"
         ELSE CONSIDER body
              WHEN `s 1196A no such body` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "connected with— (a) a foreign government or an agency or authority of a foreign government, or (b) an international organisation"
              OTHERWISE
                  IF `the name would be likely to give the false impression that the business is connected with that body`
                  THEN JUST TRUE
                  ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a name that would be likely to give the false impression"

-- src:16838 | (2) A person who contravenes this section commits an offence.
@ref s 1196A(2) Offence (src:16838)
GIVEN `the person contravenes the prohibition on a name suggesting connection with a foreign government or an international organisation` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1196A(2) the person commits an offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the person contravenes the prohibition on a name suggesting connection with a foreign government or an international organisation`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person who contravenes this section commits an offence" (the offence is defined by the contravention: marginal reading (a))
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person contravenes is not known
-- src:16839 | (3) Where an offence under this section is committed by a body corporate, an offence is also committed by every officer of the body who is in default.
@ref s 1196A(3) Offence: every officer of the body corporate who is in default (src:16839)
GIVEN `the body corporate commits an offence under this section` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1196A(3) an officer of the body corporate commits an offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the body corporate commits an offence under this section`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an offence under this section is committed by a body corporate, an offence is also committed by every officer of the body who is in default" (a "where" that fails: the 2026-11-05 ruling)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the body corporate commits the offence is not known
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        CONSIDER `s 1121 the officer is in default`
        WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an offence is also committed by every officer of the body who is in default"
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the officer is in default is the answer of s 1121
-- src:16840 | (4) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 3 on the standard scale.
@ref s 1196A(4) Penalty for an offence under s 1196A (src:16840)
GIVEN guilty IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 1196A(4) the penalty for an offence under s 1196A` MEANS
    CONSIDER guilty
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        JUST (Penalty WITH `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction`
                           `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING
                           `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 1)
                           `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 0.1)
                           `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE)
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person is guilty is not known

-- ---- s 1197: Name containing inappropriate indication of company type or legal form -----------------------------
-- The regulations prohibiting names (subsections (1), (2) and (4)) are not among the sources: whether the name is one
-- they prohibit is a plain input.

-- src:16849 | (3) In this section “specified” means specified in the regulations.
@ref s 1197(3) "Specified" (src:16849)
GIVEN `the matter is specified in the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1197(3) the matter is specified` MEANS
    IF `the matter is specified in the regulations`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In this section “specified” means specified in the regulations"

-- src:16842 | 1197 Name containing inappropriate indication of company type or legal form
-- src:16843 | (1) The Secretary of State may make provision by regulations prohibiting a person from carrying on business in the United Kingdom under a name consisting of or containing specified words, expressions or other indications—
-- src:16844 | (a) that are associated with a particular type of company or form of organisation, or
-- src:16845 | (b) that are similar to words, expressions or other indications associated with a particular type of company or form of organisation.
@ref s 1197(1) Name containing inappropriate indication of company type or legal form (src:16842-16845)
GIVEN `the person carries on business in the United Kingdom under the name` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the regulations under s 1197 prohibit the name` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1199 sections 1192 to 1197 do not apply to the business` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 1199A(1) the prohibitions of this Chapter do not apply to the business under the name` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1197(5) the person uses a name in contravention of regulations under s 1197` MEANS
    IF `s 1199 sections 1192 to 1197 do not apply to the business` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Those sections do not apply to the carrying on of a business by a person who— (a) carried on the business immediately before the date on which this Chapter came into force" (s 1199(2))
    ELSE IF `s 1199A(1) the prohibitions of this Chapter do not apply to the business under the name` EQUALS JUST TRUE
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "provide that a prohibition imposed by this Chapter does not apply in relation to the carrying on of a business by that person under a name specified in the notice" (s 1199A(1))
         ELSE IF `the person carries on business in the United Kingdom under the name` AND `the regulations under s 1197 prohibit the name`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the regulations under s 1197 decide which names are prohibited, and none is among the sources

-- src:16851 | (5) A person who uses a name in contravention of regulations under this section commits an offence.
@ref s 1197(5) Offence (src:16851)
GIVEN `s 1197(5) the person uses a name in contravention of regulations under s 1197` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1197(5) the person commits an offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 1197(5) the person uses a name in contravention of regulations under s 1197`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person who uses a name in contravention of regulations under this section commits an offence" (the offence is defined by the contravention: marginal reading (a))
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person contravenes is not known
