    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        JUST (Penalty WITH `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction`
                           `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING
                           `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 1)
                           `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 0.1)
                           `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE)
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person is guilty is not known

-- ---- s 1198: Name giving misleading indication of activities --------------------------------------------------

-- src:16854 | 1198 Name giving misleading indication of activities
-- src:16855 | (1) A person must not carry on business in the United Kingdom under a name that gives so misleading an indication of the nature of the activities of the business as to pose a risk of harm to the public in the United Kingdom or elsewhere.
@ref s 1198(1) Name giving misleading indication of activities (src:16854-16855)
GIVEN `the person carries on business in the United Kingdom under the name` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the name gives so misleading an indication of the nature of the activities of the business as to pose a risk of harm to the public in the United Kingdom or elsewhere` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1199A(1) the prohibitions of this Chapter do not apply to the business under the name` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1198(1) the person uses a name in contravention of the prohibition on a name giving a misleading indication of activities` MEANS
    IF `s 1199A(1) the prohibitions of this Chapter do not apply to the business under the name` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "provide that a prohibition imposed by this Chapter does not apply in relation to the carrying on of a business by that person under a name specified in the notice" (s 1199A(1))
    ELSE IF NOT `the person carries on business in the United Kingdom under the name`
         THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "carry on business in the United Kingdom under a name"
         ELSE IF `the name gives so misleading an indication of the nature of the activities of the business as to pose a risk of harm to the public in the United Kingdom or elsewhere`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a name that gives so misleading an indication of the nature of the activities of the business as to pose a risk of harm to the public"

