-- ---- s 1198A: Name that a company has been required to change ------------------------------------------------

DECLARE `s 1198A direction` IS ONE OF
    `s 1198A a direction under s 67`
    `s 1198A a direction under s 75`
    `s 1198A a direction under s 76`
    `s 1198A a direction under s 76A`
    `s 1198A a direction under s 76B(1)(b) given on the basis that, at the time at which the company's name was registered, the Secretary of State had proper grounds for forming the opinion mentioned in s 57A`
    `s 1198A any other direction under s 76B`
    `s 1198A another direction`

-- src:16870 | (5) In this section—
-- src:16871 | “company” includes an overseas company;
-- src:16872 | “relevant direction” means a direction under section 67, 75, 76, 76A or 76B, other than a direction under section 76B(1)(b) given on the basis that, at the time at which a company’s name was registered, the Secretary of State had proper grounds for forming the opinion mentioned in section 57A.
@ref s 1198A(5) "Relevant direction" (src:16870-16872)
GIVEN direction IS A `s 1198A direction`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1198A(5) the direction is a relevant direction` MEANS
    CONSIDER direction
    WHEN `s 1198A a direction under s 67` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 1198A a direction under s 75` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 1198A a direction under s 76` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 1198A a direction under s 76A` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 1198A any other direction under s 76B` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 1198A a direction under s 76B(1)(b) given on the basis that, at the time at which the company's name was registered, the Secretary of State had proper grounds for forming the opinion mentioned in s 57A` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“relevant direction” means a direction under section 67, 75, 76, 76A or 76B, other than a direction under section 76B(1)(b) given on the basis that, at the time at which a company’s name was registered, the Secretary of State had proper grounds for forming the opinion mentioned in section 57A" (the "(other than X)" site of the 2026-11-05 ruling: fork F6)
    WHEN `s 1198A another direction` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“relevant direction” means a direction under section 67, 75, 76, 76A or 76B"

-- src:16871 | “company” includes an overseas company;
@ref s 1198A(5) "Company" (src:16871)
GIVEN `the body is an overseas company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1198A(5) the body is a company for the purposes of s 1198A` MEANS
    IF `the body is an overseas company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“company” includes an overseas company"

-- src:16862 | (2) Subsection (1) does not prevent the use by a company of a name if—
-- src:16863 | (a) the period for complying with the direction or order has not yet expired,
-- src:16864 | (b) the company complied with the direction or order and has since become registered with the name again following approval given under section 57B, or
-- src:16865 | (c) the direction was given, or the order was made, before section 25 of the Economic Crime and Corporate Transparency Act 2023 came fully into force.
@ref s 1198A(2) Exceptions: use of the name that the company was directed or ordered to change (src:16862-16865)
GIVEN `the period for complying with the direction or order has not yet expired` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company complied with the direction or order and has since become registered with the name again following approval given under s 57B` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the direction was given, or the order was made, before s 25 of the Economic Crime and Corporate Transparency Act 2023 came fully into force` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1198A(2) subsection (1) prevents the company using the name` MEANS
    IF `the period for complying with the direction or order has not yet expired`
       OR `the company complied with the direction or order and has since become registered with the name again following approval given under s 57B`
       OR `the direction was given, or the order was made, before s 25 of the Economic Crime and Corporate Transparency Act 2023 came fully into force`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) does not prevent the use by a company of a name if— (a) the period for complying with the direction or order has not yet expired, (b) the company complied with the direction or order and has since become registered with the name again following approval given under section 57B, or (c) the direction was given, or the order was made, before section 25 of the Economic Crime and Corporate Transparency Act 2023 came fully into force"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (2) says nothing of a company to which none of (a) to (c) applies; subsection (1) decides

-- src:16860 | 1198A Name that a company has been required to change
-- src:16861 | (1) Where a relevant direction has been given to a company to change its name, or it has been ordered under section 73 to change its name, the company must not carry on business in the United Kingdom under the name that it was directed or ordered to change, except as mentioned in subsection (2).
@ref s 1198A(1) Name that a company has been required to change (src:16860-16861)
GIVEN `s 1198A(5) the direction is a relevant direction` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the company has been ordered under s 73 to change its name` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company carries on business in the United Kingdom under the name that it was directed or ordered to change` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1198A(2) subsection (1) prevents the company using the name` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 1199A(1) the prohibitions of this Chapter do not apply to the business under the name` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1198A(1) the company uses the name in contravention of s 1198A` MEANS
    IF NOT (`s 1198A(5) the direction is a relevant direction` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `the company has been ordered under s 73 to change its name`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a relevant direction has been given to a company to change its name, or it has been ordered under section 73 to change its name" (a "where" that fails: the 2026-11-05 ruling)
    ELSE IF `s 1198A(2) subsection (1) prevents the company using the name` EQUALS JUST FALSE
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the company must not carry on business in the United Kingdom under the name that it was directed or ordered to change, except as mentioned in subsection (2)"
         ELSE IF `s 1199A(1) the prohibitions of this Chapter do not apply to the business under the name` EQUALS JUST TRUE
              THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "provide that a prohibition imposed by this Chapter does not apply in relation to the carrying on of a business by that person under a name specified in the notice" (s 1199A(1))
              ELSE IF `the company carries on business in the United Kingdom under the name that it was directed or ordered to change`
                   THEN JUST TRUE
                   ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "carry on business in the United Kingdom under the name that it was directed or ordered to change"

-- src:16866 | (3) If a company uses a name in contravention of this section an offence is committed by—
-- src:16867 | (a) the company, and
-- src:16868 | (b) every officer of the company who is in default.
@ref s 1198A(3)(a) Offence: the company (src:16866-16868)
GIVEN `the company uses the name in contravention of s 1198A` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1198A(3)(a) the company commits an offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the company uses the name in contravention of s 1198A`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a company uses a name in contravention of this section an offence is committed by— (a) the company" (an "if" that is not met)
