GIVEN `the company uses the name in contravention of s 1198A` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1198A(3)(b) an officer of the company commits an offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the company uses the name in contravention of s 1198A`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a company uses a name in contravention of this section an offence is committed by— (b) every officer of the company who is in default" (a "where" that fails: the 2026-11-05 ruling)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the body corporate commits the offence is not known
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        CONSIDER `s 1121 the officer is in default`
        WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an offence is committed by ... (b) every officer of the company who is in default"
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the officer is in default is the answer of s 1121
-- src:16869 | (4) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 3 on the standard scale.
@ref s 1198A(4) Penalty for an offence under s 1198A (src:16869)
GIVEN guilty IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 1198A(4) the penalty for an offence under s 1198A` MEANS
    CONSIDER guilty
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        JUST (Penalty WITH `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction`
                           `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING
                           `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 1)
                           `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 0.1)
                           `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE)
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person is guilty is not known

-- ---- s 1198B: Name that another company has been required to change ----------------------------------------------

-- src:16888 | “company” includes an overseas company;
@ref s 1198B(7) "Company" (src:16888)
GIVEN `the body is an overseas company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1198B(7) the body is a company for the purposes of s 1198B` MEANS
    IF `the body is an overseas company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“company” includes an overseas company"

-- src:16870 | (5) In this section—
-- src:16871 | “company” includes an overseas company;
-- src:16872 | “relevant direction” means a direction under section 67, 75, 76, 76A or 76B, other than a direction under section 76B(1)(b) given on the basis that, at the time at which a company’s name was registered, the Secretary of State had proper grounds for forming the opinion mentioned in section 57A.
-- src:16887 | (7) In this section—
-- src:16888 | “company” includes an overseas company;
-- src:16889 | “relevant direction” means a direction under section 67, 75, 76A or 76B, other than a direction under section 76B(1)(b) given on the basis that, at the time at which a company’s name was registered, the Secretary of State had proper grounds for forming the opinion mentioned in section 57A.
@ref s 1198B(7) "Relevant direction" (src:16870-16889)
GIVEN direction IS A `s 1198A direction`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1198B(7) the direction is a relevant direction` MEANS
    CONSIDER direction
    WHEN `s 1198A a direction under s 67` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 1198A a direction under s 75` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 1198A a direction under s 76A` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 1198A any other direction under s 76B` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 1198A a direction under s 76` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“relevant direction” means a direction under section 67, 75, 76A or 76B" (s 76 is not in the list of s 1198B(7), unlike s 1198A(5): a finding)
    WHEN `s 1198A a direction under s 76B(1)(b) given on the basis that, at the time at which the company's name was registered, the Secretary of State had proper grounds for forming the opinion mentioned in s 57A` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "other than a direction under section 76B(1)(b) given on the basis that, at the time at which a company’s name was registered, the Secretary of State had proper grounds for forming the opinion mentioned in section 57A" (the "(other than X)" site of the 2026-11-05 ruling: fork F6)
    WHEN `s 1198A another direction` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“relevant direction” means a direction under section 67, 75, 76A or 76B"

DECLARE `s 1198B relationship of the person to the company` IS ONE OF
    `s 1198B an officer`
    `s 1198B a member or former member`
    `s 1198B another relationship`

-- src:16880 | (4) For the purposes of this section a person has a “relevant relationship” with a company if the person is—
-- src:16881 | (a) an officer, or
-- src:16882 | (b) a member or former member.
@ref s 1198B(4) "Relevant relationship" (src:16880-16882)
GIVEN relationship IS A `s 1198B relationship of the person to the company`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1198B(4) the person has a relevant relationship with the company` MEANS
    CONSIDER relationship
    WHEN `s 1198B another relationship` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a person has a “relevant relationship” with a company if the person is— (a) an officer, or (b) a member or former member"
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- Subsection (3): whether the person has, or has had, the relationship with both companies at the same time is irrelevant.
-- src:16874 | (1) Where a relevant direction has been given to a company to change its name, or it has been ordered under section 73 to change its name, another company must not carry on business in the United Kingdom under the name that the first company was directed or ordered to change if there is a person who has, or has had, a relevant relationship with both companies.
-- src:16879 | (3) For the purposes of subsection (1) it is irrelevant whether the person has, or has had, a relevant relationship with both companies at the same time.
@ref s 1198B(3) It is irrelevant whether the person has or had the relationships at the same time (src:16874-16879)
GIVEN `s 1198B(4) the person has a relevant relationship with the company, or has had one, with the first company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 1198B(4) the person has a relevant relationship with the company, or has had one, with the second company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1198B(3) there is a person who has, or has had, a relevant relationship with both companies` MEANS
    IF `s 1198B(4) the person has a relevant relationship with the company, or has had one, with the first company` EQUALS JUST TRUE
       AND `s 1198B(4) the person has a relevant relationship with the company, or has had one, with the second company` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE -- whether the two relationships were held at the same time is irrelevant (s 1198B(3))
    ELSE IF `s 1198B(4) the person has a relevant relationship with the company, or has had one, with the first company` EQUALS JUST FALSE
            OR `s 1198B(4) the person has a relevant relationship with the company, or has had one, with the second company` EQUALS JUST FALSE
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if there is a person who has, or has had, a relevant relationship with both companies" (an "if" that is not met)
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the s 1198B(4) answer for one of the companies is not known

-- src:16875 | (2) Subsection (1) does not prevent the use by a company of a name if—
-- src:16876 | (a) it is registered under this Act by that name,
-- src:16877 | (b) the period for complying with the direction or order has not yet expired, or
-- src:16878 | (c) the direction was given, or the order was made, before section 26 of the Economic Crime and Corporate Transparency Act 2023 came fully into force.
@ref s 1198B(2) Exceptions: use of the name by another company (src:16875-16878)
GIVEN `the other company is registered under the Companies Act 2006 by that name` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the period for complying with the direction or order has not yet expired` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the direction was given, or the order was made, before s 26 of the Economic Crime and Corporate Transparency Act 2023 came fully into force` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1198B(2) subsection (1) prevents the other company using the name` MEANS
    IF `the other company is registered under the Companies Act 2006 by that name`
       OR `the period for complying with the direction or order has not yet expired`
       OR `the direction was given, or the order was made, before s 26 of the Economic Crime and Corporate Transparency Act 2023 came fully into force`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) does not prevent the use by a company of a name if— (a) it is registered under this Act by that name, (b) the period for complying with the direction or order has not yet expired, or (c) the direction was given, or the order was made, before section 26 of the Economic Crime and Corporate Transparency Act 2023 came fully into force"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (2) says nothing of a company to which none of (a) to (c) applies; subsection (1) decides

-- src:16873 | 1198B Name that another company has been required to change
-- src:16874 | (1) Where a relevant direction has been given to a company to change its name, or it has been ordered under section 73 to change its name, another company must not carry on business in the United Kingdom under the name that the first company was directed or ordered to change if there is a person who has, or has had, a relevant relationship with both companies.
@ref s 1198B(1) Name that another company has been required to change (src:16873-16874)
GIVEN `s 1198B(7) the direction is a relevant direction` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the first company has been ordered under s 73 to change its name` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other company carries on business in the United Kingdom under the name that the first company was directed or ordered to change` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1198B(3) there is a person who has, or has had, a relevant relationship with both companies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 1198B(2) subsection (1) prevents the other company using the name` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 1199A(1) the prohibitions of this Chapter do not apply to the business under the name` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1198B(1) the other company uses the name in contravention of s 1198B` MEANS
    IF NOT (`s 1198B(7) the direction is a relevant direction` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `the first company has been ordered under s 73 to change its name`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a relevant direction has been given to a company to change its name, or it has been ordered under section 73 to change its name" (a "where" that fails: the 2026-11-05 ruling)
    ELSE IF `s 1198B(3) there is a person who has, or has had, a relevant relationship with both companies` EQUALS JUST FALSE
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "another company must not carry on business in the United Kingdom under the name ... if there is a person who has, or has had, a relevant relationship with both companies"
         ELSE IF `s 1198B(2) subsection (1) prevents the other company using the name` EQUALS JUST FALSE
              THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) does not prevent the use by a company of a name if— ..."
              ELSE IF `s 1199A(1) the prohibitions of this Chapter do not apply to the business under the name` EQUALS JUST TRUE
                   THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "provide that a prohibition imposed by this Chapter does not apply in relation to the carrying on of a business by that person under a name specified in the notice" (s 1199A(1))
                   ELSE IF `the other company carries on business in the United Kingdom under the name that the first company was directed or ordered to change`
                           AND `s 1198B(3) there is a person who has, or has had, a relevant relationship with both companies` EQUALS JUST TRUE
                        THEN JUST TRUE
                        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "another company must not carry on business in the United Kingdom under the name that the first company was directed or ordered to change if there is a person who has, or has had, a relevant relationship with both companies"

-- src:16883 | (5) If a company uses a name in contravention of this section an offence is committed by—
-- src:16884 | (a) the company, and
-- src:16885 | (b) every officer of the company who is in default.
@ref s 1198B(5)(a) Offence: the company (src:16883-16885)
GIVEN `the other company uses the name in contravention of s 1198B` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1198B(5)(a) the company commits an offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the other company uses the name in contravention of s 1198B`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a company uses a name in contravention of this section an offence is committed by— (a) the company" (an "if" that is not met)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the company uses the name in contravention is not known
-- src:16883 | (5) If a company uses a name in contravention of this section an offence is committed by—
-- src:16884 | (a) the company, and
-- src:16885 | (b) every officer of the company who is in default.
@ref s 1198B(5)(b) Offence: every officer of the company who is in default (src:16883-16885)
GIVEN `the other company uses the name in contravention of s 1198B` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1198B(5)(b) an officer of the company commits an offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the other company uses the name in contravention of s 1198B`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a company uses a name in contravention of this section an offence is committed by— (b) every officer of the company who is in default" (a "where" that fails: the 2026-11-05 ruling)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the body corporate commits the offence is not known
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        CONSIDER `s 1121 the officer is in default`
        WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an offence is committed by ... (b) every officer of the company who is in default"
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the officer is in default is the answer of s 1121
-- src:16886 | (6) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 3 on the standard scale.
@ref s 1198B(6) Penalty for an offence under s 1198B (src:16886)
GIVEN guilty IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 1198B(6) the penalty for an offence under s 1198B` MEANS
    CONSIDER guilty
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        JUST (Penalty WITH `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction`
                           `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING
                           `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 1)
                           `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 0.1)
                           `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE)
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person is guilty is not known

-- ---- s 1199: Savings for existing lawful business names -------------------------------------------------------

DECLARE `s 1199 provision` IS ONE OF
    `s 1199 a section from s 1192 to s 1196`
    `s 1199 s 1197`
    `s 1199 another provision`

-- src:16891 | 1199 Savings for existing lawful business names
-- src:16892 | (1) This section has effect in relation to—
-- src:16893 | sections 1192 to 1196 (sensitive words or expressions), and
-- src:16894 | section 1197 (inappropriate indication of company type or legal form).
@ref s 1199(1) The sections s 1199 has effect in relation to (src:16891-16894)
GIVEN provision IS A `s 1199 provision`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1199(1) the saving has effect in relation to the provision` MEANS
    CONSIDER provision
    WHEN `s 1199 another provision` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "This section has effect in relation to— sections 1192 to 1196 ..., and section 1197" is not closed with "only" (s 1196A, s 1198, s 1198A and s 1198B are not named: a finding)
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:16895 | (2) Those sections do not apply to the carrying on of a business by a person who—
-- src:16896 | (a) carried on the business immediately before the date on which this Chapter came into force, and
-- src:16897 | (b) continues to carry it on under the name that immediately before that date was its lawful business name.
@ref s 1199(2) Business carried on before the date on which this Chapter came into force (src:16895-16897)
GIVEN `the person carried on the business immediately before the date on which this Chapter came into force` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person continues to carry it on under the name that immediately before that date was its lawful business name` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1199(2) sections 1192 to 1197 do not apply to the business` MEANS
    IF `the person carried on the business immediately before the date on which this Chapter came into force`
       AND `the person continues to carry it on under the name that immediately before that date was its lawful business name`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Those sections do not apply to the carrying on of a business by a person who— (a) carried on the business immediately before the date on which this Chapter came into force, and (b) continues to carry it on under the name that immediately before that date was its lawful business name"

-- "during the period of twelve months beginning with the date of the transfer": the first day of the period is the date of
-- the transfer, and the period ends on the day before the same date a year later (fork F11: the library's `add months`
-- clamps a day that does not exist, so a transfer on 29 February is not tested).
-- src:16898 | (3) Where—
-- src:16899 | (a) a business is transferred to a person on or after the date on which this Chapter came into force, and
-- src:16900 | (b) that person carries on the business under the name that was its lawful business name immediately before the transfer,
-- src:16901 | those sections do not apply in relation to the carrying on of the business under that name during the period of twelve months beginning with the date of the transfer.
@ref s 1199(3) A business transferred on or after the date on which this Chapter came into force (src:16898-16901)
GIVEN `the business is transferred to the person on or after the date on which this Chapter came into force` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person carries on the business under the name that was its lawful business name immediately before the transfer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the transfer` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the business is carried on under that name` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1199(3) sections 1192 to 1197 do not apply to the business carried on under that name on the date` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the business is transferred to the person on or after the date on which this Chapter came into force`
            AND `the person carries on the business under the name that was its lawful business name immediately before the transfer`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where— (a) a business is transferred to a person on or after the date on which this Chapter came into force, and (b) that person carries on the business under the name that was its lawful business name immediately before the transfer"
    ELSE IF `the date on which the business is carried on under that name` AT LEAST `the date of the transfer`
            AND `the date on which the business is carried on under that name` LESS THAN (`add months` `the date of the transfer` 12)
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "those sections do not apply in relation to the carrying on of the business under that name during the period of twelve months beginning with the date of the transfer" (outside the period the text fixes in its own words: the 2026-11-05 ruling)

DECLARE `s 1199 time at which the business was carried on under the name` IS ONE OF
    `s 1199 before this Chapter came into force`
    `s 1199 after this Chapter came into force`

-- src:16902 | (4) In this section “lawful business name”, in relation to a business, means a name under which the business was carried on without contravening—
-- src:16903 | (a) section 2(1) of the Business Names Act 1985 (c. 7) or Article 4(1) of the Business Names (Northern Ireland) Order 1986 (S.I. 1986/1033 N.I. 7)), or
-- src:16904 | (b) after this Chapter has come into force, the provisions of this Chapter.
@ref s 1199(4) "Lawful business name" (src:16902-16904)
GIVEN `when the business was carried on under the name` IS A `s 1199 time at which the business was carried on under the name`
      `the business was carried on in contravention of s 2(1) of the Business Names Act 1985 or Article 4(1) of the Business Names (Northern Ireland) Order 1986` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the business was carried on in contravention of the provisions of this Chapter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1199(4) the name is a lawful business name` MEANS
    CONSIDER `when the business was carried on under the name`
    WHEN `s 1199 before this Chapter came into force` THEN
        IF `the business was carried on in contravention of s 2(1) of the Business Names Act 1985 or Article 4(1) of the Business Names (Northern Ireland) Order 1986`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“lawful business name”, in relation to a business, means a name under which the business was carried on without contravening— (a) section 2(1) of the Business Names Act 1985 or Article 4(1) of the Business Names (Northern Ireland) Order 1986"
        ELSE JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 1199 after this Chapter came into force` THEN
        IF `the business was carried on in contravention of the provisions of this Chapter`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“lawful business name”, in relation to a business, means a name under which the business was carried on without contravening— (b) after this Chapter has come into force, the provisions of this Chapter"
        ELSE JUST TRUE

-- ---- s 1199A: Exceptions based on national security etc --------------------------------------------------

-- src:16905 | 1199A Exceptions based on national security etc
-- src:16906 | (1) The Secretary of State may, by written notice given to a person, provide that a prohibition imposed by this Chapter does not apply in relation to the carrying on of a business by that person under a name specified in the notice, if satisfied that to do so is necessary—
-- src:16907 | (a) in the interests of national security, or
-- src:16908 | (b) for the purposes of preventing or detecting serious crime.
@ref s 1199A(1) Exceptions based on national security etc (src:16905-16908)
GIVEN `the Secretary of State has given the person written notice specifying the name and providing that a prohibition imposed by this Chapter does not apply to the carrying on of the business under it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary of State is satisfied that it is necessary in the interests of national security` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary of State is satisfied that it is necessary for the purposes of preventing or detecting serious crime` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1199A(1) the prohibitions of this Chapter do not apply to the business under the name` MEANS
    IF `the Secretary of State has given the person written notice specifying the name and providing that a prohibition imposed by this Chapter does not apply to the carrying on of the business under it`
       AND (`the Secretary of State is satisfied that it is necessary in the interests of national security`
            OR `the Secretary of State is satisfied that it is necessary for the purposes of preventing or detecting serious crime`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The Secretary of State may, by written notice given to a person, provide that a prohibition imposed by this Chapter does not apply in relation to the carrying on of a business by that person under a name specified in the notice, if satisfied that to do so is necessary— (a) in the interests of national security, or (b) for the purposes of preventing or detecting serious crime"

-- src:16909 | (2) For the purposes of subsection (1)(b)—
-- src:16910 | (a) “crime” means conduct which—
-- src:16911 | (i) constitutes a criminal offence, or
-- src:16912 | (ii) is, or corresponds to, any conduct which, if it all took place in any one part of the United Kingdom, would constitute a criminal offence, and
@ref s 1199A(2)(a) "Crime" (src:16909-16912)
GIVEN `the conduct constitutes a criminal offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the conduct is, or corresponds to, conduct which, if it all took place in any one part of the United Kingdom, would constitute a criminal offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1199A(2)(a) the conduct is crime` MEANS
    IF `the conduct constitutes a criminal offence` OR `the conduct is, or corresponds to, conduct which, if it all took place in any one part of the United Kingdom, would constitute a criminal offence`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“crime” means conduct which— (i) constitutes a criminal offence, or (ii) is, or corresponds to, any conduct which, if it all took place in any one part of the United Kingdom, would constitute a criminal offence"

-- src:16913 | (b) crime is “serious” if—
-- src:16914 | (i) the offence which is or would be constituted by the conduct is an offence for which the maximum sentence (in any part of the United Kingdom) is imprisonment for 3 years or more, or
-- src:16915 | (ii) the conduct involves the use of violence, results in substantial financial gain or is conduct by a large number of persons in pursuit of a common purpose.
@ref s 1199A(2)(b) "Serious" crime (src:16913-16915)
GIVEN `the longest maximum term of imprisonment, in years, that the offence carries in any part of the United Kingdom` IS A NUMBER
      `the conduct involves the use of violence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the conduct results in substantial financial gain` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the conduct is conduct by a large number of persons in pursuit of a common purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1199A(2)(b) the crime is serious` MEANS
    IF `the longest maximum term of imprisonment, in years, that the offence carries in any part of the United Kingdom` AT LEAST 3
       OR `the conduct involves the use of violence`
       OR `the conduct results in substantial financial gain`
       OR `the conduct is conduct by a large number of persons in pursuit of a common purpose`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "crime is “serious” if— (i) the offence which is or would be constituted by the conduct is an offence for which the maximum sentence (in any part of the United Kingdom) is imprisonment for 3 years or more, or (ii) the conduct involves the use of violence, results in substantial financial gain or is conduct by a large number of persons in pursuit of a common purpose"
